Reproducer originally authored by w8; independently read, compiled and run by w4.

$ rustc docs/reviews/w8-evidence/unbounded_read.rs -o /tmp/gds-w4-protocol-6HfPaU/unbounded_read
exit code: 0
$ (ulimit -v 131072; timeout 5s /tmp/gds-w4-protocol-6HfPaU/unbounded_read /dev/zero)
read error: out of memory
exit code: 0

The reproducer prints std::fs::read errors and exits normally. This demonstrates
unbounded reading exhausting the child virtual-memory allowance. It is not a
full GUI run, a demonstrated process abort, or proof of local data exfiltration.
